        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Italian media reports US top diplomat Rubio to meet Pope Leo Italy Issued on: 03/05/2026 - 17:26 Modified: 03/05/2026 - 17:26 Marco Rubio will travel to Rome this week for a visit reportedly aimed at easing strained relations with the Italyn government and the Holy See. Both Giorgia Meloni and Pope Leo XIV have faced criticism from Donald Trump, who has publicly attacked the pontiff’s anti-war remarks. Marco Rubio is due to be in the Italian capital during the first anniversary of Pope Leo XIV’s papacy, the first US-born leader of the Catholic Church. France 24 correspondent Seema Gupta reports the latest from Rome. Venice Biennale jury resigns against participation of Russia and Israel 01/05/2026 Italy Trump-Meloni relationship turns sour 17/04/2026 Americas Day of zero waste: International Chef Massimo Bottura speaks to France 24 29/03/2026 Italy Milan Cortina opening ceremony's best moments 07/02/2026 Italy Milan-Cortina Winter Olympic Games to kick off Friday 05/02/2026 Italy Angel resembling Italy's PM Meloni painted over after ouctry 05/02/2026 Italy 'Capitalist logic of Olympics: Sponsored by fossil fuels while pledging sustainability' 05/02/2026 Sport Milan-Cortina Winter Games kick off on Friday: Olympic torch relay in final stretch 04/02/2026 Italy Milan-Cortina Olympic Games: Some venues still not finished 04/02/2026 Italy"
